{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_f462d6fkmjnlvb2ofletw6ncztiwmzia424uo3xnmsh5pe3fcj6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All 30 tests pass under every feature combination.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single translation unit exporting one symbol: `void driver(int x, int y)` — a `while` loop with two `goto` labels (one forward-skip, one backwards jump) that prints `\"loop\"`, `\"x\"`, `\"y\"` lines. The Rust translation was already functionally correct; I did not need to change `src/lib.rs` at all.\n\n## Phase A artifacts (`translation/`)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly one dynamic symbol (`driver`); Rust `.so` exports it too. Symbol diff is empty; all Rust undefined symbols are libc/unwind. No C module was skipped (verified: `driver.c` defines only `driver`, no statics/macro symbols).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — grepping for every rejection construct found **none**: no `return`, `assert`, `NULL`, error enum, or range check exists. So the table enumerates the 13 executable \"rejection-like\" behaviours (guard-false → silent return, the `INT_MIN` corners, arbitrary out-of-range/enum-shaped ints) plus 2 documented non-executable rows.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 20 rows over the 5 branch axes (guard, the `x==1 && y==4` skip, `x>0`, `y==0` continue, `x<3` back-goto) × input shapes, including a near-exhaustive `[-6,40]²` grid.\n\n## Two real problems I found and fixed — both in the harness, not the C\n\n1. **Stale-library blind spot (critical).** `cargo test` does **not** build a `cdylib`-only lib target, so the tests were loading a `.so` left over from an earlier `cargo build --release`. I proved this by mutation testing: six semantic mutations of `src/lib.rs` were **all** passed silently. The harness now builds the cdylib itself into `target/so-under-test` and asserts the artifact is newer than `src/lib.rs`. After the fix, all six mutations are detected by multiple rows.\n2. **fd-1 capture races.** Captures redirect file descriptor 1 process-wide, so libtest's own progress text leaked into captures. Fixed by pinning `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` (`.cargo/config.toml`), flushing Rust's line-buffered stdout before redirecting, and refusing to run if concurrency was re-enabled.\n\n## Two input regions deliberately not executed (C-side limits, documented)\n\n- `x > 0 && y < 0`: the C decrements `y` forever (it never equals `0`), so it never terminates and overflows — **UB in C**, unbounded output.\n- `x.max(0) + y.max(0)` near `INT_MAX`, e.g. `(INT_MAX, 0)`: terminates only after ~2³¹ iterations. An early version of my suite actually hit `SIGXFSZ` here; the harness now refuses these and `configs_row17` asserts they are the refused ones.\n\nRun everything with `cd translation && ./verify.sh` (builds the C reference, loops all feature combinations — there are no `[features]`, so default and `--no-default-features` — and diffs `nm -D`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2403,"cache_read_input_tokens":89481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2403,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05620088-d450-4b98-875a-334ebbd21110","uuid":"2a07c806-d289-4499-ae87-7ec8b6530862","timestamp":"2026-08-28T14:01:57.408Z"}
